a master’s degree (or equivalent) in computer science, engineering, mathematics, physics, economics, finance, statistics or another relevant field (see How you can join us [https://www.ecb.europa.eu/careers/before-you-apply/html/index.en.html] for details on degree equivalences);
in addition to the above, a minimum of four years’ experience in designing digital workplace solutions;
excellent analytical, drafting and presentation skills, with the ability to explain complex topics to diverse audiences;
an advanced (C1) command of English and an intermediate (B1) command of at least one other official language of the EU, according to the Common European Framework of Reference for Languages [https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/table-1-cefr-3.3-common-reference-levels-global-scale].

Desired:

highly skilled in driving alignment across IT disciplines to identify and prioritise user needs in relation to the operational, security, reliability, cost and sustainability dimensions and in delivering outcomes at enterprise scale;
experience of successfully managing and delivering workplace solutions and modernising legacy products in close collaboration with a managed service provider;
experience describing and presenting detailed technical designs and architectures, as well as functional roadmaps;
solid knowledge of security-by-design in the digital workplace, such as Zero Trust, identity and access management, endpoint security, information protection, data loss prevention and privacy and regulatory requirements;
hands-on experience with M365 and other standards from the Microsoft suite;
understanding of AI-enabled workplace capabilities and other emerging technologies, including Microsoft Copilot, and the associated security, data governance and adoption considerations.

You are motivated to contribute to the ECB’s mission, to serve the citizens of the EU as a member of a public institution and to work with colleagues from all over Europe. You are motivated to be part of our team and to develop and use your skills and competencies to achieve the aims of this position. You are aware of your strengths and areas for development and know what motivates you to perform at your highest level.

